From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: complete stock memory reservations

Comparing the HD1913 stock reserved-memory union with the mainline hotdog
tree leaves two stock-owned intervals visible to the Linux page allocator:

  - 0x89b00000-0x89d00000 from removed_regions
  - 0x99517000-0x99600000 from cdsp_regions

The second full DDR capture was taken after the XBL/AOP gap fix. It found
Flatpak page-cache folios from the crashing staging inode at
0x99518000-0x99580000, inside the omitted CDSP interval. This reproduces the
same firmware ownership collision at the next missing reservation.

Reserve both remaining intervals as no-map. Together with the preceding
XBL/AOP fix, this makes the mainline reserved-memory union cover every byte
owned by the enabled HD1913 stock reservations.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -96,6 +96,16 @@ / {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		stock_removed_gap: memory@89b00000 {
+			reg = <0 0x89b00000 0 0x200000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		stock_cdsp_gap: memory@99517000 {
+			reg = <0 0x99517000 0 0xe9000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		hotdog_removed_gap: hotdog-removed-gap@89d00000 {
 			reg = <0 0x89d00000 0 0x1a00000>;
 			no-map;
-- 
